-- ============================================================================
-- DR7 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Cementing, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the volume sheet, which is cylinder arithmetic on
-- lengths and diameters. The annulus as a list of capacity rows cut at the
-- section boundaries and the shoe and NOWHERE else, so the top of cement and
-- the lead and tail split are handled by overlapping the rows rather than by
-- splitting one. The inside as a single capacity of 0.01937743444976952 square
-- metres, because the string is one size. Six inputs refused BY NAME rather
-- than guessed at, including a liner job, which the engine says belongs to a
-- later phase. Four volumes: the annular slurry between the top of cement and
-- the shoe, the shoe track which is pumped and deliberately never placed, the
-- lead and tail split which moves no total, and the displacement measured to
-- the FLOAT COLLAR rather than the shoe.
--
-- THE FINDING THE MODULE IS BUILT ON, AND IT IS ABOUT ONE INPUT. Walk the
-- inputs to a volume sheet and every one is a measurement, a published table
-- or a design decision, except the OPEN HOLE EXCESS, which is a guess. Every
-- other uncertainty on the sheet is in the third or fourth significant figure
-- and this one is in the first. The excess multiplies the open hole capacity
-- ONLY, the effective bore is back-solved from the inflated capacity rather
-- than assumed, and the slurry volume is exactly linear in it. At the
-- published 15 percent the washed-out open hole reads 0.22104932820526735 m
-- against a cased bore of 0.2204974, so the open hole annulus is WIDER than
-- the cased one it hangs from, and at the bit size it was narrower. Getting
-- the excess 15 points low costs 2.8274277333640363 cubic metres of annular
-- slurry, which is about 212 m of uncemented annulus at the top.
--
-- A SECOND FINDING, IN m05. The two published wells have IDENTICAL slurry
-- volumes, to the last digit: 24.34828356497546 annular, 0.7750973779907808
-- shoe track, 657.6801293970221 sacks. One is a 40 degree slant to 3000 m and
-- the other a horizontal well with a 1600 m lateral, and their shoe true
-- vertical depths differ by nearly 1300 m. The volume sheet cannot tell them
-- apart, because it is a function of LENGTHS and diameters and inclination
-- enters nowhere. Their displacements differ by 3.875486889953905 cubic
-- metres, which is 200 m of casing bore, and that is the only number on the
-- whole sheet that distinguishes them.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling cementing module against cementing_cases.json, and the
-- teaching lab the panels and this course share is pinned by
-- cementingLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all 505
-- literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an engine-derived
-- value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks reports zero
-- downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all eighteen
-- graded fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('cementing', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-primary-cement-job-is","title":"What a Primary Cement Job Is","lesson_keys":["l01-why-a-well-is-cemented","l02-the-four-things-the-job-must-do","l03-shoe-float-collar-plugs-spacer","l04-what-this-engine-models"]},{"key":"m02-the-geometry","title":"The Geometry","lesson_keys":["l01-two-tubulars-and-a-hole","l02-annulus-capacity-rows","l03-where-the-rows-are-cut","l04-inside-capacity","l05-where-the-geometry-refuses"]},{"key":"m03-open-hole-excess","title":"Open Hole Excess","lesson_keys":["l01-the-hole-is-not-the-bit","l02-the-excess-factor","l03-the-effective-bore","l04-what-excess-costs","l05-excess-is-the-biggest-guess"]},{"key":"m04-the-volumes","title":"The Volumes","lesson_keys":["l01-top-of-cement","l02-annular-slurry","l03-the-shoe-track","l04-lead-and-tail","l05-displacement"]},{"key":"m05-sacks-time-and-the-sheet","title":"Sacks, Time and the Sheet","lesson_keys":["l01-yield-and-sacks","l02-job-time","l03-two-wells-one-slurry-volume","l04-what-a-volume-sheet-hides"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
